---
source: tests/golden/harness.rs
---
  x `signed` needs #true or #false
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-bases/collections/two/colour.base.kdl:6:5]
 5 |     provides "Rechunking" "/usr/bin/flatpak"
 6 |     signed "yes"
   :     ^^^|^^
   :        `-- not a boolean
 7 |     colour "red"
   `----
  help: `signed #true` records that this base publishes a cosign signature

  x unknown node `colour` in a base
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-bases/collections/two/colour.base.kdl:7:5]
 6 |     signed "yes"
 7 |     colour "red"
   :     ^^^|^^
   :        `-- not part of the schema
 8 |     bootloader "grub2"
   `----
  help: a base entry holds `image`, `about`, `family`, `provides`, `requires`,
        `signed`, `scap-content` and `bootloader`: what an image built on it
        may assume, what it still needs, what a person picks it by, what
        measures it and what it boots with

  x invalid capability name `Rechunking`
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-bases/collections/two/colour.base.kdl:5:5]
 4 |     family "fedora"
 5 |     provides "Rechunking" "/usr/bin/flatpak"
   :     ^^^^|^^^
   :         `-- lowercase, digits and dashes, starting with a letter
 6 |     signed "yes"
   `----
  help: the name is written into the generated graph as a mermaid label and a
        markdown table cell, neither of which quotes anything

  x `/usr/bin/flatpak` is a path where a capability is named
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-bases/collections/two/colour.base.kdl:5:5]
 4 |     family "fedora"
 5 |     provides "Rechunking" "/usr/bin/flatpak"
   :     ^^^^|^^^
   :         `-- a name, such as `ssh` or `bootc`
 6 |     signed "yes"
   `----
  help: a capability is found at `/usr/bin/<name>` or `/usr/sbin/<name>`;
        anywhere else, a module writes `provides "<name>" file="<path>"`, or a
        capabilities library a `capability "<name>" { path "<path>" }` row

  x `base` declares no `about`
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-bases/collections/two/no-about.base.kdl:1:1]
 1 | base {
   : ^^|^
   :   `-- nothing to pick it by
 2 |     image "example.invalid/no-about:1"
   `----
  help: `about "..."` is the line `tect create image` shows beside the
        reference

  x `base` describes no `family`
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-bases/collections/two/no-family.base.kdl:1:1]
 1 | base {
   : ^^|^
   :   `-- no family
 2 |     image "example.invalid/no-family:1"
   `----
  help: the family is what an image scaffolded on this base declares, and an
        entry without one describes nothing the tool can write

  x this base names no `image`
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-bases/collections/two/nothing-named.base.kdl:1:1]
 1 | base {
   : ^^|^
   :   `-- no image reference
 2 |     about "Nothing names it"
   `----
  help: the reference the build starts from, such as `image "quay.io/fedora/
        fedora-bootc:44"`

  x `example.invalid/shared:1` is described by two base files
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-bases/collections/two/shared.base.kdl:1:1]
 1 | base {
   : ^^|^
   :   `-- `tests/repos/broken-bases/collections/one/shared.base.kdl` describes it too
 2 |     image "example.invalid/shared:1"
   `----
  help: one image reference is one base: two files would each write a
        different family and a different `provides` into an image scaffolded
        on it, and which one did would depend on the order the sources are
        read in

  x this `family` block names no path
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-bases/collections/caps/capabilities.kdl:10:5]
  9 | capability "familyless" {
 10 |     family "fedora" "debian"
    :     ^^^|^^
    :        `-- nothing to read
 11 | }
    `----
  help: `family "debian" { path "/usr/bin/ssh" }`, the file the family is
        checked for

  x `usr/bin/flatpak` is not an absolute path
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-bases/collections/caps/capabilities.kdl:1:1]
 1 | capability "flatpak" {
   : ^^^^^|^^^^
   :      `-- an absolute path
 2 |     path "usr/bin/flatpak"
   `----
  help: the path is checked on the finished image, where nothing has a working
        directory

  x invalid capability name `Bad Name`
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-bases/collections/caps/capabilities.kdl:5:1]
 4 | 
 5 | capability "Bad Name" {
   : ^^^^^|^^^^
   :      `-- lowercase, digits and dashes, starting with a letter
 6 |     path "/usr/bin/x"
   `----
  help: the name is written into the generated graph as a mermaid label and a
        markdown table cell, neither of which quotes anything
